  "疑惑中真正的安稳不在于环境顺利，而在于与耶稣的关系；把疑惑带到神面前，借着祂的话语重新认识祂的同在、供应和大能，疑惑就能成为信心受塑造的契机。": "True security in doubt comes from a relationship with Jesus, rather than favorable circumstances. Bringing doubts to God and rediscovering His presence, provision, and power through His Word can make doubt an occasion for faith to grow.",
  "以下为依据讲道的综合解读，非讲员逐字引语。讲员借《诗篇》第73篇指出，亚萨因注视恶人的兴盛而嫉妒，进而怀疑服侍神是否值得；进入神的圣所后，他才重新认识恶人的结局，以及神同在的宝贵。讲员再借《马可福音》第4章的风暴故事说明，疑惑可以被带到耶稣面前，成为门徒信心受塑造的过程。信息最终邀请听众谨慎处理疑惑，先亲近神、聆听祂的话语，并在圣餐中记念耶稣的受死、复活与同在的应许。": "The following is a synthesis of the sermon, not a verbatim quotation. Through Psalm 73, the speaker shows how Asaph's envy of the wicked's prosperity led him to question whether serving God was worthwhile. Entering God's sanctuary changed his understanding of their end and the value of God's presence. The storm in Mark 4 then illustrates how doubts brought to Jesus can become part of the disciples' growth in faith. The message invites listeners to handle doubt carefully, draw near to God and listen to His Word first, and remember Jesus' death, resurrection, and promised presence in Communion.",
  "一、人生不稳时，安全感从哪里来": "1. Where do we find security when life is unstable?",
  "半圆顶登山经历引出人生需要稳固支撑的问题。": "A climb on Half Dome introduces the need for firm support in life.",
  "亚萨虽知道神良善，却因看见恶人兴盛而几乎失去方向。": "Although Asaph knew God was good, seeing the wicked prosper almost caused him to lose his way.",
  "二、目光中的比较，如何成为心中的疑惑": "2. How comparison becomes doubt",
  "山地骑行的经历说明，注视的方向会影响前进的方向。": "A mountain-biking experience illustrates how the direction of our gaze shapes where we go.",
  "讲员将亚萨的嫉妒解释为渴望恶人看似拥有的平安，并质疑神是否把福分赐错了对象。": "The speaker interprets Asaph's envy as a longing for the apparent peace of the wicked and a question about whether God had blessed the wrong people.",
  "选择性比较会滋生苦毒，使人误以为神没有供应自己。": "Selective comparison breeds bitterness and can make us believe God has failed to provide for us.",
  "三、承认疑惑，同时留意处理疑惑的方式": "3. Acknowledge doubt and consider how you handle it",
